  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n8 (1)/(4) + 2 (1)/(3) + 4 (2)/(3) - 6 (1)/(4)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nConvert mixed fractions to improper fractions, perform addition/subtraction, and convert back to mixed fractions if required.\n\n**Calculation:**\n\n8 (1)/(4) = (33)/(4), 2 (1)/(3) = (7)/(3), 4 (2)/(3) = (14)/(3), 6 (1)/(4) = (25)/(4)\n\nExpression becomes:\n\n(33)/(4) + (7)/(3) + (14)/(3) - (25)/(4)\n\nTake LCM of 4 and 3 = 12\n\n(33)/(4) = (99)/(12), (7)/(3) = (28)/(12), (14)/(3) = (56)/(12), (25)/(4) = (75)/(12)\n\nExpression becomes:\n\n(99)/(12) + (28)/(12) + (56)/(12) - (75)/(12)\n\nAdd/subtract numerators:\n\n(99 + 28 + 56 - 75)/(12) = (108)/(12)\n\nSimplify:\n\n(108)/(12) = 9\n\n**∴ The value of 8 (1)/(4) + 2 (1)/(3) + 4 (2)/(3) - 6 (1)/(4) is 9.**",
